                "text": "**Analyzing Pixel Distributions**\n\nI've been examining the pixel distributions along a central column. For instance, I noted the four \"8\" pixels in column 7 of the example. Now, I'm working through how to translate this vertical count into the specified horizontal output of pixels.\n\n\n**Discovering Pyramid Structures**\n\nI've realized the vertical counts translate to pyramid rows in the horizontal output. For instance, a count of 4 for the color \"8\" becomes a row of width 1 and a row of width 3. This pyramid structure seems consistent across examples. The order from top to bottom of output matches the layers as well! The examples support this interpretation, and it's starting to make sense.\n\n\n**Confirming Pyramid Logic**\n\nI'm now certain the pyramid logic is correct and working from bottom to top, stacking rows of increasing widths. In Example 2, the bottom row of width 5, color 5, is followed by width 3, color 7, and width 1, color 4. In Example 3, color 8 makes up the bottom row of width 3, and then color 6 makes up the top row of width 1. The examples show the bottom-up construction perfectly. It's becoming clearer with each test!\n\n\n",
